it is the end of an era as the last  smash ultimate character has finally  been revealed  we're gonna talk about that and how  kingdom hearts is coming to switch how  you can get into the battlefield 2042  beta early and how ghost recon is  getting a new mode my name is devonte  chisholm and you're watching gamespot  news  now i know we're all heartbroken that cj  from san andreas didn't make it into  smash ultimate but let's put that  heartbreak aside because the guy that  did make it is pretty cool mr sakurai  revealed sora of the kingdom hearts  series as the game's final dlc character  and the majority of the 40-minute  presentation was dedicated to showing  off his moves stage musical selections  and more the presentation also unveiled  the last batch of downloadable me  fighter costumes which include  doomslayer from doom as well as an  octoling wig and jut the cat hat from  splatoon these me fighter costumes will  be available on october 18th for 75  cents each and as if those announcements  weren't enough sakurai also announced  that nintendo and square enix are  teaming up to launch three kingdom  hearts games on nintendo switch and  these names are all a mouthful so bear  with me here we go kingdom hearts hd 1.5  plus 2.5 remix kingdom hearts hd 2.8  final chapter prologue and kingdom  hearts 3. these will all be cloud games  that stream to your switch aka you will  need a constant internet connection to  play them  but okay let's talk about some shooter  news now battlefield 2042's open beta is  right around the corner and is now  available to preload the beta will kick  off on october 6th for those who have  pre-ordered the game or subscribe to ea  play everyone else can play starting on  october 8th until the beta ends on  october 10th adding to this dice has  published an faq that runs down the key  details of what you need to know about  the battlefield 2042 open beta and  preloading for instance it will not show  up automatically in your game library  you will need to search for battlefield  2042 open beta on your chosen storefront  and in other shooter related news  ubisoft has announced ghost recon  frontline a large-scale pvp shooter that  carries the tactical heritage of the  shooter but implements it in a first  person multiplayer experience the  standard gameplay mode in frontline  expedition pits 100 players against each  other in small teams of three-person  squads their objective is to find  crucial intel and extract it but must  contend with the other squads to do so  the action takes place on the island of  drakemore which was described as being  four by four kilometer in size and  features four distinct biomes and 20  landmarks one of the key gameplay  considerations that ubisoft hopes will  distinguish frontline from other battle  royale games is the ability to change  the battlefield players will be able to  earn and deploy equipment weapons and  gadgets however specific items such as  turrets cover and even a sniper tower  can also be dropped in  but i remember far cry 2's villain the  jackal well during an interview with ign  far cry 2's creative director clint  hawking confirmed that jack carver the  protagonist from fc1 was definitely the  jackal this confirmation puts a lid on a  13 year old fan theory so if you were  one of those people that was speculating  all these years then congrats you can  rest  and speaking of far cry the sixth  installment is so close to its official  release and similar to fc four and five  far cry 6 features a secret ending that  can be unlocked early in the story to do  this you'll need to get on the boat and  you only have one chance to do this and  drive in the opposite direction of your  objective that's all super simple i  can't wait to play this game and i  wonder which ending i'm gonna like more  so go ahead and hit the comment section  and let me know how hype you are for  sora on a scale of 1 to 10  and if it could have been a different  character who would you have wanted let  me know  peace  [Music]  you
 

